cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: article
title: "Statistical Inference for Series Systems from Masked Failure Time Data: The Exponential Case"
authors:
  - family-names: "Towell"
    given-names: "Alexander"
    email: "atowell@siue.edu"
    affiliation: "Southern Illinois University Edwardsville"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6443-0618"
abstract: >-
  We consider the problem of estimating component failure rates in series
  systems when observations consist of system failure times paired with
  partial information about the failed component. For the case where
  component lifetimes follow exponential distributions, we derive
  closed-form expressions for the maximum likelihood estimator, the
  Fisher information matrix, and establish sufficient statistics. The
  asymptotic sampling distribution of the estimator is characterized
  and confidence intervals are provided.
keywords:
  - maximum likelihood estimation
  - Fisher information matrix
  - masked system failure time
  - series systems
  - exponential distribution
  - sufficient statistics
  - reliability engineering
  - competing risks
